title: -- as end-of-options separator is not honoured, so option-shaped titles need
  --title
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

Found while filing another ticket: a title starting with `--` cannot be passed
positionally, and the POSIX escape hatch for exactly that does not work.

    karr create "--dir makes set-refs unreachable"
      -> usage dump, rc=2                      # parsed as options
    karr create -- "--dir positional after separator"
      -> "Title is required. Use --title or pass as argument."   # -- not honoured
    karr create --title "--dir makes set-refs unreachable"
      -> works

Being unable to pass an option-shaped positional is normal; having no `--` is
not. Every CLI is expected to honour it, and an agent generating task titles
from arbitrary text (error messages, flags, diffs) will hit this. The workaround
exists but is undiscoverable — the error message does mention `--title`, which
is the one saving grace.

Affects every command that takes a positional, not just `create`.

Fix: let MooX::Options/Getopt see `--` as the end of options (`getopt_conf` with
`require_order`/`pass_through` as appropriate), and add a test that a title of
`--json` survives a round trip.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
